cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below, and cite EuroSAT separately."
title: "TerraScope: an accuracy-energy benchmark for land-cover classification on CPU-only hardware"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/eklavya072/TerraScope-GeoSpatial-AI"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible benchmark of the accuracy-energy trade-off for EuroSAT land-cover
  classification on CPU-only hardware. Five architectures x five seeds under one
  identical training recipe, exported to ONNX at fp32 and int8, measured for
  accuracy (mean with 95% confidence intervals), latency, memory and energy
  through ONNX Runtime's CPU execution provider against a committed,
  hash-identified data split.
keywords:
  - remote sensing
  - land cover classification
  - EuroSAT
  - benchmark
  - energy efficiency
  - quantization
references:
  - type: article
    title: "EuroSAT: A Novel Dataset and Deep Learning Benchmark for Land Use and Land Cover Classification"
    authors:
      - family-names: Helber
        given-names: Patrick
      - family-names: Bischke
        given-names: Benjamin
      - family-names: Dengel
        given-names: Andreas
      - family-names: Borth
        given-names: Damian
